<title>TURKEY: Turkish Aksa 1996 net profits double.</title>
<headline>Turkish Aksa 1996 net profits double.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final results</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)   1,822.15  vs    1,618.00</p>
<p>    Net profit		    6,082.87  vs    2,842.99</p>
<p>    Net sales		    28,312.79  vs   18,698.42</p>
<p>    Operating Profits	   7,395.37  vs    4,152.96</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  2,483.77  vs    1,123.47</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	   479.61  vs	360.23</p>
<p>    Interest Paid		   465.97  vs	375.16</p>
<p>    Total debts		   5,699.05  vs    4,120.33</p>
<p>    Equity			 13,638.84  vs    7,413.46</p>
<p>    Capital			 3,338.30  vs    1,757.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Acrylic based tow and fibre producer Aksa Akrilik Kimya Sanayii A.S. is owned largely by Akkok textile group.</p>
<p>The company plans to pay 850 lira dividend per 1,000 lira nominal valued share from its 1996 profits after approval at the annual meeting of shareholders and directors.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent wholesale inflation in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
